<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rupert of Salzburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 710</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Saint Rupert</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rupert of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> was a Frankish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> and missionary, probably from Worms, who worked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in the late 7th and early 8th centuries. Invited by Duke Theodo, he founded a church and the monastery of St Peter at the ruined Roman town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iuvavum">Iuvavum</a> around 696, and the convent of Nonnberg. Venerated as a saint, he is the patron of the city and state of Salzburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rupert-of-salzburg.jpg" alt="Rupert of Salzburg" width="273" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rupert-Salzburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
